Patches applied on top of the pristine upstream tarball by
scripts/vendor-webrtc-apm.sh, in filename order.

This directory is empty by design. The upstream patches/ directory of
webrtc-audio-processing (MinGW fixes, MSVC winsock2/XMM fixes, BSD support)
is a record of deltas that are already applied in the v2.1 release tree, so
the cgo/MinGW build needs nothing on top of it. Verified against v2.1:
rtc_base/system/file_wrapper.cc and rtc_base/logging.cc already include
<windows.h> in lower case with <winsock2.h> first, and
rtc_base/platform_thread_types.cc already guards the structured-exception
thread naming with #ifndef __MINGW32__.
